and for our our hymnium loving audience how it affected or didn't affect how I met your mother and of course how it led to this book.
对于我们钟爱“Hymium”的听众来说，它对《老爸老妈的浪漫史》产生了什么影响（或者没有影响），当然，又是如何促成了这本书的诞生。

00:13:10.717 --> 00:13:26.712
I want to pause for one second that's a great question but I also want to say that Elliot my son who is in one of one of the inspirations for Emmett in the book he's watching and chiming in with questions and comments and he just wrote am I the second star of the book?
我想暂停一下，这是一个非常好的问题，但我也想说，我的儿子埃利奥特——他也是书中埃米特的灵感来源之一——他正在观看并用问题和评论参与进来，他刚刚写道：我是书中的男二号吗？

00:13:26.712 --> 00:13:33.490
He wants to be co-star along with Emmett fictional Emmett and real-life Elliot are the the two stars of this book.
他想成为联合主演，虚构的埃米特和现实生活中的埃利奥特是这本书的两位主角。

00:13:33.490 --> 00:13:41.101
And I'm going to go ahead and say that, yes, Elliot, you are definitely one of the stars of this book in so many different ways.
我要提前说一句，是的，埃利奥特，你绝对是这本书的主角之一，以各种不同的方式。

00:13:41.101 --> 00:13:47.820
But to flash back him in style back to 2007, as you just pointed out, yeah, it was a game changer on every level.
但以“Hymium”的方式闪回到2007年，正如你刚才所指出的，是的，那在各个层面都是一个转折点。

00:13:47.820 --> 00:13:50.447
It was a game changer for my whole life.
它改变了我整个人生。

00:13:50.447 --> 00:13:53.600
It was a game changer for how I met your mother.
它改变了《老爸老妈的浪漫史》。

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:57.644
We had no idea that we were about to have a child with a disability.
我们当时完全不知道我们将要迎来一个残疾的孩子。

00:13:57.644 --> 00:14:00.379
Nothing showed up on testing that we had done.
我们做过的检查显示一切正常。

00:14:00.379 --> 00:14:05.969
He had this very rare chromosomal deletion that led to some heart issues and the heart issues.
他患有一种非常罕见的染色体微缺失，导致了一些心脏问题。

00:14:05.969 --> 00:14:28.687
Once he was born, that's how we found out there was a genetic syndrome because he was in immediate distress because of these heart issues that were also too small to see at the time in 2007 on the types of scans that were available then because they involved these teeny tiny little veins being not wired the right way in his heart and he needed open heart surgery at two weeks old.
他出生后，我们才发现存在遗传综合征，因为这些心脏问题让他立刻陷入痛苦。在2007年当时的扫描技术下，这些问题也太小而无法看到，因为它们涉及他心脏中像牙签一样细小的血管没有正确连接，他在两周大时就需要做开胸手术。

00:14:28.687 --> 00:14:31.601
He was born much smaller than anyone had thought.
他的出生体重比任何人想象的都要小得多。

00:14:31.601 --> 00:14:42.009
So many things we didn't know, and we're just total surprises, and he weighed about 3.8 pounds, 11 ounces, and needed open heart surgery to fix veins the size of dental floss.
有太多我们不知道的事情，完全是意料之外，他体重只有约3磅11盎司（约1.68公斤），需要做开胸手术来修复牙线大小的血管。

00:14:42.009 --> 00:14:44.566
And it was, as you can imagine, 50-50 odds.
你可以想象，当时只有五成把握。

00:14:44.566 --> 00:14:46.945
You know, he could have gone either way.
你知道的，情况可能会走向任何一个方向。

00:14:46.945 --> 00:14:58.779
And we followed his lead, and he proved that he wanted to be here and has done so every day since, including to today, as he's sitting there chiming and saying he's the star of the book, which he is.
我们顺应着他的意愿，而他证明了自己想要留在这个世界，从那以后每天都如此，直到今天，他正坐在那里插话，说他是这本书的主角，他确实是。

00:14:58.779 --> 00:15:02.860
And yeah, but what did it do to my life at that time, what did it do to How Much Mother?
是的，但这对当时我的生活有什么影响，对《老爸老妈的浪漫史》有什么影响？

00:15:02.860 --> 00:15:05.179
It was between year two and three of How Much Mother.
那是《老爸老妈的浪漫史》第二年和第三年之间。

00:15:05.179 --> 00:15:17.299
It was during the hiatus between those two seasons and the way that young parents arrogantly think, we're just going to bang out a perfectly fine kid and then I'll just be right back to work.
那是两季之间的间歇期，带着年轻父母那种傲慢的想法，我们生一个完美健康的小孩，然后我马上就能回去工作了。

00:15:17.299 --> 00:15:18.299
It's perfect.
这太完美了。

00:15:18.299 --> 00:15:29.799
If just right in the middle of the hiatus, perfectly scheduled, right back in when we We ran up the writer's room in the late spring, you know, after Elliot was born April 30th and maybe in late May or whatever it was going to be, we were going to round it back up and good.
正好在间歇期中间，时间安排得天衣无缝，我们在春末重新组建编剧室，你知道的，在埃利奥特4月30日出生之后，大概在5月下旬或无论什么时候，我们就要重新开工了，一切都会很好。

00:15:29.799 --> 00:15:31.559
And it would all be easy and I'll go according to plan.
一切都会很简单，按计划进行。

00:15:31.559 --> 00:15:36.320
And it was, of course, not bad and it turned out to be very humbling.
当然，事情并非如此，结果证明这让我们感到非常卑微。

00:15:36.320 --> 00:15:49.320
Right off the bat having, because we were in the NICU, the neonatal intensive care unit for about six weeks and then we got Elliot home and spent every second of being home terrified too.
一开始，因为我们在NICU（新生儿重症监护室）呆了大约六周，然后把埃利奥特接回家，在家的每一秒也都感到惊恐万分。

00:15:49.320 --> 00:15:56.656
the NICU, then constantly like, oh, but there's no team of nurses and equipment to make sure he's okay here at our home.
离开NICU后，总是会想：哦，但是家里没有护士团队和设备来确保他在这里的安全。

00:15:56.656 --> 00:16:02.403
And you almost want to go back to the NICU, even those baddies you wanted to get out of there.
你甚至想回到NICU，尽管那些坏事曾让你迫不及待地想离开那里。

00:16:02.403 --> 00:16:07.966
But we began this hugely steep learning curve, my wife, Rebecca and I, Rebecca was amazing.
但我和我的妻子丽贝卡开始了这段极其陡峭的学习曲线，丽贝卡太棒了。

00:16:07.966 --> 00:16:12.001
An amazing mom at figuring everything out to me to be figured out.
她是一位出色的妈妈，把所有需要弄明白的事情都弄明白了。

00:16:12.001 --> 00:16:19.399
And she didn't have what I had, which was the ability after a few weeks to head into how I met your mother writer's room.
她没有我所拥有的那种特权——几周后就能去《老爸老妈的浪漫史》的编剧室工作。

00:16:19.399 --> 00:16:21.539
And that was such an escape for me.
对我来说，那真是一种解脱。

00:16:21.539 --> 00:16:26.797
And I use that word escape because that does factor into the book a little bit, right?
我用“解脱”这个词，因为这确实在一定程度上影响了这本书，对吧？

00:16:26.797 --> 00:16:44.159
The idea of which parent really stays the most in the discomfort of solving all of these problems, confronting all of these huge world-shaking twists and turns of being the parent of a medically complicated kid who also has a a rare syndrome and it's gonna have learning disabilities.
关于哪个父母能更多地停留在解决所有这些问题的不适感中，去面对抚养一个患有罕见综合征、身体状况复杂且将会有学习障碍的孩子所带来的那些震撼世界的波折。

00:16:44.159 --> 00:16:59.240
And I got to go in to a writer's room and make dick jokes for a very significant portion of the early months of Elliot's life and got to go in and spend time with Ted and Robin and Marshall and Lily and that world.
而我却可以走进编剧室，在埃利奥特生命最初几个月的大部分时间里讲一些下流的笑话，去和泰德、罗宾、马歇尔、莉莉以及那个世界度过时光。

00:16:59.240 --> 00:17:03.000
And I would say for me, it was so healing to have that.
我会说，对我而言，拥有那样一个世界是极具治愈效果的。

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:14.289
That's my first answer to your rationale, because it was so, I was very lucky to have another world to spend time in, besides the real world of our lives, that was really hard.
这是我对你那个问题的第一个回答，因为太好了，我非常幸运能拥有另一个世界去度过时光，除了我们生活中那个非常艰难的现实世界。

00:17:14.289 --> 00:17:18.930
And then when I would go back to that world, Rebecca, my wife, of course, had been in that world all day long.
然后当我回到现实世界时，我的妻子丽贝卡，当然已经在那个世界（现实）呆了一整天。

00:17:18.930 --> 00:17:23.450
And it was really hard and that dynamic stayed with me.
那真的很艰难，这种动态关系一直留在我心中。

00:17:23.450 --> 00:17:35.609
And that is something I write about in the book, the idea of it's so hard for couples in this position because one person has to sacrifice more and spend more time in the really hard part.
这也是我在书中写到过的，对于处在这个位置的伴侣来说真的很艰难，因为其中一个人必须作出更多牺牲，并在真正艰难的部分投入更多时间。

00:17:35.609 --> 00:17:42.170
And the other one has to go make money to pay for everything that's going on at home and medically and everything for the whole future.
而另一个人则必须去赚钱，来支付家里发生的一切、医疗费用以及整个未来的所有开销。

00:17:42.170 --> 00:17:50.690
But that person, even though they're under enormous pressure to provide financially, they still get to go do something else with part of the day.
但那个人，尽管承受着巨大的经济供给压力，一天中仍然有一部分时间可以去做别的事情。

00:17:50.690 --> 00:17:57.970
And I'd say that was a really, that's what comes back to me when you say what did spring of 2007 feel like, that's where that was.
我想说，这真的是……当你问我2007年春天是什么感觉时，浮现出我脑海的正是这些。

00:17:57.970 --> 00:17:58.809
Yeah.
是啊。

